WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.160 --> 00:00:02.170
- [Mark] All right, Monika.

00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:03.003
- [Monika] Yes.

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:04.760
- [Mark] Monika, you work for a firm

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:06.720
that helps out a lot of the
people that I interview, right?

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:07.553
- [Monika] I do.

00:00:07.553 --> 00:00:09.470
I work for Patrick Cady Foundation.

00:00:09.470 --> 00:00:11.720
- [Mark] And what do you guys do exactly?

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:14.540
- So we find people 25 and under

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:19.260
that are in need of support
in getting off of drugs,

00:00:19.260 --> 00:00:20.620
getting off the street.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:22.710
We sponsor them.

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:26.570
We get them through detox,
residential, sober living,

00:00:26.570 --> 00:00:27.690
vocational training.

00:00:27.690 --> 00:00:30.350
We get them back into
school if they want it.

00:00:30.350 --> 00:00:32.080
Throughout the recovery process,

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:33.950
people kind of move
through a lot of things

00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:34.783
they want to do.

00:00:34.783 --> 00:00:37.270
So we work with them
until they get solid on

00:00:37.270 --> 00:00:39.930
what they see for themselves
and then we go there.

00:00:39.930 --> 00:00:40.763
- [Mark] That's great.

00:00:40.763 --> 00:00:44.173
So some of the people that
my viewers respond to,

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:48.840
like Christina and Maddie and
some of the younger people,

00:00:48.840 --> 00:00:50.810
would be prime candidates
for what you guys do, right?

00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:52.700
- They would be wonderful candidates.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:55.638
I want to help them (laughs)

00:00:55.638 --> 00:00:56.471
Yeah.

00:00:56.471 --> 00:00:57.304
- [Mark] Yeah, that's great.

00:00:57.304 --> 00:01:02.304
And then the GoFundMe campaign
that I started recently,

00:01:03.260 --> 00:01:06.793
which a portion is designed
to help some of these people.

00:01:07.930 --> 00:01:12.800
So far I think we're at
around $20,000, which is nice,

00:01:12.800 --> 00:01:17.360
but I'm concerned that maybe
that's just not gonna solve

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:18.600
these peoples' problems.

00:01:18.600 --> 00:01:20.240
Especially if we're spreading this $20,000

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:23.093
over 20 people or more.

00:01:24.297 --> 00:01:27.530
That buys Maddie a new tent
and Christina some clothes

00:01:27.530 --> 00:01:29.660
and a tent and stuff like that.

00:01:29.660 --> 00:01:33.790
It doesn't change the
direction of their lives.

00:01:33.790 --> 00:01:34.780
- It doesn't.

00:01:34.780 --> 00:01:38.390
Just to give context,
putting someone through detox

00:01:38.390 --> 00:01:41.890
is $550 a day on average in California.

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:46.890
So that's just the 7-10
days to get them off

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:50.960
what they're on, that's
not the residential

00:01:50.960 --> 00:01:53.370
which keeps them off
and starts to do therapy

00:01:53.370 --> 00:01:54.600
and that kind of stuff.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:57.837
So when you do the math, it
costs, without insurance,

00:01:57.837 --> 00:02:02.837
$35,000-40,000 to get
somebody clean and sober

00:02:02.980 --> 00:02:04.730
and safe for a solid amount of time.

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:06.670
You have to think most people
are gonna have hiccups,

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:08.480
so they gotta go back to detox.

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:10.530
It's very rare that we
get somebody into detox

00:02:10.530 --> 00:02:11.780
and they don't use again.

00:02:13.360 --> 00:02:17.110
So it adds up really fast
and even with insurance,

00:02:17.110 --> 00:02:21.310
sometimes things are covered
but it's short stays,

00:02:21.310 --> 00:02:26.310
it's not the full distance
that someone has to go

00:02:26.765 --> 00:02:29.050
to get clean and stay clean

00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:31.200
by any stretch of the imagination.

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:33.500
- [Mark] I have a lot of subscribers

00:02:33.500 --> 00:02:34.370
or viewers to my channel

00:02:34.370 --> 00:02:36.230
and if everybody that
watched my channel donated

00:02:36.230 --> 00:02:38.980
the minimum amount, we could
do everything you're describing

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:40.460
and more, for everybody, really.

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:43.468
But I don't know if that's
really in the cards.

00:02:43.468 --> 00:02:44.830
- I hope so (laughs)

00:02:44.830 --> 00:02:47.870
- [Mark] That'd be great, but
it seems like a lot of people

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:49.900
don't really have what it takes to help.

00:02:49.900 --> 00:02:53.170
And a lot of my donors to this
campaign have been amazing.

00:02:53.170 --> 00:02:57.953
There's some people that
donated $2500, one person did,

00:02:58.787 --> 00:03:00.850
and there's a few donated
$1000 and a lot of $500s

00:03:00.850 --> 00:03:03.367
and things like that and that's amazing.

00:03:03.367 --> 00:03:05.266
Very, very grateful for those donors.

00:03:05.266 --> 00:03:07.240
- Yeah, that's great (laughs)

00:03:07.240 --> 00:03:08.410
- [Mark] But we still
don't have a million people

00:03:08.410 --> 00:03:09.930
donating the minimum
which would really make

00:03:09.930 --> 00:03:10.970
a huge difference, right?

00:03:10.970 --> 00:03:14.389
- That's what it takes and listen,

00:03:14.389 --> 00:03:18.200
with the donations you have,
you can get feminine products,

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:21.060
you can get tents, we can
go get mass amounts of food

00:03:21.060 --> 00:03:22.410
and feed people.

00:03:22.410 --> 00:03:25.210
But if it were that easy, if it took $1000

00:03:25.210 --> 00:03:27.190
to get somebody off the
streets and off drugs,

00:03:27.190 --> 00:03:30.010
well, most people wouldn't
be in the position they're in

00:03:30.010 --> 00:03:31.140
because think about some of the women

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:32.920
that you're interviewing,
how much money they can make

00:03:32.920 --> 00:03:33.770
in a day.

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:37.840
If it were that easy, they
wouldn't be in this position.

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:38.673
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:03:38.673 --> 00:03:40.060
So you guys have been around for how long?

00:03:40.060 --> 00:03:40.893
How many years?

00:03:40.893 --> 00:03:41.726
- Four years now.

00:03:41.726 --> 00:03:42.559
- [Mark] Four years?

00:03:42.559 --> 00:03:45.520
And you're based right
down the street from me.

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:47.640
Basically you're around
the edge of skid row.

00:03:47.640 --> 00:03:48.603
- Yeah, yup.

00:03:52.500 --> 00:03:54.550
- [Mark] So you're a non-profit.

00:03:54.550 --> 00:03:56.030
- Yes.

00:03:56.030 --> 00:04:00.030
- [Mark] And you can only
handle so many people at once.

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:03.060
It's not like you have 400
people that you're fixing, right?

00:04:03.060 --> 00:04:04.590
- Yeah, yeah.

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:06.610
- [Mark] How many people
typically do you take in?

00:04:06.610 --> 00:04:09.610
- Well, it just depends
on my personal capacity

00:04:09.610 --> 00:04:11.270
as well as Nashay's and Jim's.

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:13.070
Because we're really small right now,

00:04:13.070 --> 00:04:15.390
the less people we hire, the
less people we have to pay,

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:16.900
the more people we can help.

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:19.690
But you have to think when
you're spending that much time,

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:21.970
you know, you spend a lot
of time with these people

00:04:21.970 --> 00:04:23.760
and they have your cell phone number,

00:04:23.760 --> 00:04:28.760
it's taxing and worth it, but
still taxing to be of support

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:30.210
in the way that these people need

00:04:30.210 --> 00:04:32.040
because a lot of these
people have never had anyone

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:32.873
care about them.

00:04:32.873 --> 00:04:36.650
So the journey is exhausting
for both the person

00:04:36.650 --> 00:04:37.790
going through recovery

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:39.470
and the person assisting them in that.

00:04:39.470 --> 00:04:42.280
So the caseworker aspect of it.

00:04:42.280 --> 00:04:47.280
So if we can get more funding
and I can bring in more people

00:04:48.220 --> 00:04:50.290
that can work with people
through their journeys,

00:04:50.290 --> 00:04:51.280
the sky's the limit.

00:04:51.280 --> 00:04:55.520
But again, you have to pay
somebody more often than not,

00:04:55.520 --> 00:04:58.560
to be willing to work full
time and help these people.

00:04:58.560 --> 00:05:02.160
But I can take two to three
people a year right now

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:04.550
because it takes about
a year to get somebody

00:05:04.550 --> 00:05:05.550
through the process.

00:05:07.050 --> 00:05:08.107
- [Mark] Aside from the
people that I interview,

00:05:08.107 --> 00:05:12.220
how would you find someone,
how would they sign up

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:14.900
for your program and how
would they pay for it?

00:05:14.900 --> 00:05:17.690
- Well, we have a website
with an application on it

00:05:17.690 --> 00:05:18.993
that Nashay helped set up.

00:05:21.290 --> 00:05:24.110
In terms of paying for it, it
doesn't cost them anything.

00:05:24.110 --> 00:05:27.090
The whole point of what
we're doing is helping people

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:29.773
who can't pay for this
kind of stuff themselves.

00:05:31.520 --> 00:05:34.100
So it's really just as simple
as going on the website,

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:36.590
filling out an application,
being super authentic

00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:41.420
on your application because you
gotta be ready for recovery,

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:44.347
you gotta want it, you
gotta be done, done, done.

00:05:44.347 --> 00:05:45.180
- [Mark] That's the number
one thing on the list

00:05:45.180 --> 00:05:46.170
of things needed, right?

00:05:46.170 --> 00:05:47.003
- Yeah, yeah.

00:05:47.003 --> 00:05:48.729
And a lot of people are-

00:05:48.729 --> 00:05:50.341
- [Mark] Because a lot of
people say they want it

00:05:50.341 --> 00:05:51.174
but they can't follow through.

00:05:51.174 --> 00:05:53.020
- And when they're coming
down from their high

00:05:53.020 --> 00:05:57.360
or whatever, they do want it,
they mean what they're saying,

00:05:57.360 --> 00:05:59.820
but they have to want it 24 hours a day,

00:05:59.820 --> 00:06:02.570
seven days a week because
when you stop using,

00:06:02.570 --> 00:06:04.680
all of the demons, all the memories,

00:06:04.680 --> 00:06:06.870
everything comes rushing back

00:06:06.870 --> 00:06:08.610
and that's so overwhelming.

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:09.510
And then you're in a place

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:10.850
where you don't really know anybody

00:06:10.850 --> 00:06:13.630
and the only person you
have is me or Narshay or Jim

00:06:13.630 --> 00:06:14.980
and we're on the outside.

00:06:14.980 --> 00:06:17.880
So we're there for you
but we can't hold you

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:18.713
when you're sleeping.

00:06:18.713 --> 00:06:22.720
So it's intimidating and
that's why a lot of people

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:23.553
go back to it.

00:06:23.553 --> 00:06:25.250
Because it's really scary.

00:06:25.250 --> 00:06:28.550
People typically use drugs
because they're trying to escape

00:06:28.550 --> 00:06:29.943
something really painful.

00:06:31.673 --> 00:06:33.590
- [Mark] Yeah, the broken
childhood is the beginning

00:06:33.590 --> 00:06:34.480
of it all, right?

00:06:34.480 --> 00:06:35.313
- Mm-hmm (affirmative).

00:06:35.313 --> 00:06:36.380
Most of the people on your channel.

00:06:36.380 --> 00:06:40.080
Everyone I've worked with
had a terrible childhood.

00:06:40.080 --> 00:06:41.310
- [Mark] That's why the
first question I ask

00:06:41.310 --> 00:06:43.570
is basically, tell me
about your childhood.

00:06:43.570 --> 00:06:44.743
- Right, exactly.

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:47.480
- [Mark] And have you had success stories?

00:06:47.480 --> 00:06:48.560
- Yes.

00:06:48.560 --> 00:06:49.393
Yeah.

00:06:50.470 --> 00:06:52.750
One of my most recent graduates, Manu,

00:06:52.750 --> 00:06:56.503
is now in school for music production.

00:06:58.220 --> 00:07:01.660
It took a while, he had
a number of relapses,

00:07:01.660 --> 00:07:03.570
but we stuck with him.

00:07:03.570 --> 00:07:05.603
He's been sober for about a year now.

00:07:07.410 --> 00:07:09.960
He actually wants to come back
and work for the foundation

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:12.410
when he's done with school,
which is really cool.

00:07:13.821 --> 00:07:16.410
That's my most recent, yeah.

00:07:16.410 --> 00:07:17.540
- [Mark] That's great.

00:07:17.540 --> 00:07:18.440
- We have others, but ...

00:07:18.440 --> 00:07:19.273
- [Mark] Yeah.

00:07:22.600 --> 00:07:24.180
I think a lot of viewers
will make a comment,

00:07:24.180 --> 00:07:25.590
oh, just go to rehab
and everything's fine,

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:27.650
but what I've seen, and
I'm sure you've seen it

00:07:27.650 --> 00:07:31.250
same as I have because I've
been doing this for a long time,

00:07:31.250 --> 00:07:34.640
there's so many other factors
that are just not working

00:07:34.640 --> 00:07:36.200
in these individuals.

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:37.560
They don't understand how to trust others,

00:07:37.560 --> 00:07:39.390
they don't understand how
to communicate sometimes,

00:07:39.390 --> 00:07:42.000
they don't understand how to handle money,

00:07:42.000 --> 00:07:43.009
they don't understand-

00:07:43.009 --> 00:07:43.842
- No.

00:07:43.842 --> 00:07:44.680
- [Mark] They get money in their pocket,

00:07:44.680 --> 00:07:45.690
that means they get to spend it.

00:07:45.690 --> 00:07:46.910
- Right!

00:07:46.910 --> 00:07:47.840
- [Mark] They don't know saving.

00:07:47.840 --> 00:07:51.540
None of them have bank
accounts or drivers licenses.

00:07:51.540 --> 00:07:52.373
- Right.

00:07:53.300 --> 00:07:55.040
- [Mark] They don't know
how to be responsible.

00:07:55.040 --> 00:07:57.535
They haven't been responsible for ever.

00:07:57.535 --> 00:07:59.464
- What example have they
had most of the time?

00:07:59.464 --> 00:08:00.963
- [Mark] Yeah, so it's a long ...

00:08:00.963 --> 00:08:05.030
- And that's, again, why you
have to really want recovery

00:08:05.030 --> 00:08:07.680
because it is a beast.

00:08:07.680 --> 00:08:11.150
Manu, his license was expired,
his passports expired,

00:08:11.150 --> 00:08:12.960
he doesn't have this,
he doesn't have that.

00:08:12.960 --> 00:08:15.570
I had to go to the college,
because they wouldn't admit him

00:08:15.570 --> 00:08:17.720
because of his record, I
had to go to the college

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:20.750
and petition with the board
to get him into the school.

00:08:20.750 --> 00:08:25.750
It's a lot of work to get
out and he has a good family,

00:08:27.310 --> 00:08:30.760
but it's still a lot of
work to get out of it.

00:08:30.760 --> 00:08:32.440
And then, you have to think about too,

00:08:32.440 --> 00:08:34.770
there's a lot going on
in the recovery community

00:08:34.770 --> 00:08:35.603
that's questionable.

00:08:35.603 --> 00:08:40.603
So my foundation, we vet
the detox and residential

00:08:40.900 --> 00:08:44.080
and sober living places that
we're sending our clients to

00:08:45.160 --> 00:08:48.620
and we have to because so
much of the recovery game

00:08:48.620 --> 00:08:50.330
is bodies in beds.

00:08:50.330 --> 00:08:53.020
So even if someone off
the street just goes

00:08:53.020 --> 00:08:55.900
I'm gonna go to this detox
center, I'm gonna try it,

00:08:55.900 --> 00:08:57.500
what's the likelihood
that there aren't drugs

00:08:57.500 --> 00:08:58.333
in the facility?

00:08:58.333 --> 00:08:59.980
That people aren't taking
advantage of people

00:08:59.980 --> 00:09:00.813
in the facility?

00:09:00.813 --> 00:09:01.653
It's slim.

00:09:03.100 --> 00:09:04.500
It's a broken system.

00:09:05.360 --> 00:09:08.810
- [Mark] Let's say I
wanted to take a portion

00:09:08.810 --> 00:09:10.660
of the donations that have
come in on this GoFundMe

00:09:10.660 --> 00:09:14.608
on my channel and give it to you guys

00:09:14.608 --> 00:09:16.680
and maybe if Christina's onboard

00:09:16.680 --> 00:09:17.940
we could take Christina over there

00:09:17.940 --> 00:09:20.440
and maybe you guys could help her,

00:09:20.440 --> 00:09:21.740
if that all works for her,

00:09:23.710 --> 00:09:26.690
that could potentially help
her tremendously, right?

00:09:26.690 --> 00:09:27.610
- Yes.

00:09:27.610 --> 00:09:28.663
- [Mark] What would you do?

00:09:29.862 --> 00:09:30.740
You would get her high school?

00:09:30.740 --> 00:09:32.360
- Well, we need to work on the GED.

00:09:32.360 --> 00:09:34.310
First we have to make sure she's sober,

00:09:34.310 --> 00:09:35.840
so that's step number one.

00:09:35.840 --> 00:09:39.040
The other thing that has to
happen at the same time for her

00:09:39.040 --> 00:09:41.870
is clarity on her parental situation

00:09:41.870 --> 00:09:43.070
because she is underage.

00:09:43.070 --> 00:09:46.100
So we have to find an
attorney that's willing

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:48.380
to take her case to make sure

00:09:48.380 --> 00:09:52.230
that we're doing all the
stuff we're doing properly

00:09:52.230 --> 00:09:54.660
so that we don't put
ourselves or you or her

00:09:54.660 --> 00:09:56.380
in any type of dangerous situation

00:09:56.380 --> 00:09:57.810
or uncomfortable situation.

00:09:57.810 --> 00:10:00.430
And then after she's clean,

00:10:00.430 --> 00:10:04.420
then we go to GED, then we go from there.

00:10:04.420 --> 00:10:05.253
What does she want?

00:10:05.253 --> 00:10:07.520
What does life look like
now that you understand

00:10:07.520 --> 00:10:09.880
that you are cared for and
you do have possibility?

00:10:09.880 --> 00:10:10.990
- [Mark] So it might be some job training

00:10:10.990 --> 00:10:11.823
or something like that?

00:10:11.823 --> 00:10:14.378
- Whatever she wants, I'll
make it happen (laughs)

00:10:14.378 --> 00:10:15.500
- [Mark] That's wonderful.

00:10:15.500 --> 00:10:16.660
- Yeah.

00:10:16.660 --> 00:10:17.493
- [Mark] That's great.

00:10:17.493 --> 00:10:18.465
- Yeah.

00:10:18.465 --> 00:10:21.030
- [Mark] Now maybe
viewers can understand why

00:10:22.840 --> 00:10:26.180
a robust support of a thing like this

00:10:26.180 --> 00:10:28.920
can do a lot of good but other than that,

00:10:28.920 --> 00:10:30.670
it'll be like we help Christina
and then everyone else

00:10:30.670 --> 00:10:32.720
is left high and dry when I
think we have the potential

00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:35.270
to help a lot of people
that you see on my channel.

00:10:37.200 --> 00:10:39.150
There's others coming up and
there's some in the past,

00:10:39.150 --> 00:10:41.750
Maddie, a bunch of others,
that could really benefit

00:10:42.898 --> 00:10:46.678
but you can only handle so much
and as you see with lawyers,

00:10:46.678 --> 00:10:49.920
with housing, with everything,
it gets very expensive.

00:10:49.920 --> 00:10:52.440
- It does get very expensive
and then there's also,

00:10:52.440 --> 00:10:54.470
the final aspect which we
spoke about the other day,

00:10:54.470 --> 00:10:56.910
which is the mental health aspect

00:10:56.910 --> 00:11:00.210
because some of these
people have undiagnosed,

00:11:00.210 --> 00:11:04.930
misdiagnosed, correctly
diagnosed, situations

00:11:04.930 --> 00:11:06.420
that are very challenging.

00:11:06.420 --> 00:11:11.240
If someone has schizophrenia,
there's another layer

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:13.047
that's compounded on.

00:11:13.047 --> 00:11:16.450
I've seen comments like 5150 them.

00:11:16.450 --> 00:11:20.410
Well, that's a 72 hour
hold and our system's

00:11:20.410 --> 00:11:22.080
gonna put them back into the world.

00:11:22.080 --> 00:11:23.930
- [Mark] And the police won't do a 5150.

00:11:23.930 --> 00:11:25.260
- Even if they do it at all, yeah.

00:11:25.260 --> 00:11:27.230
- [Mark] I couldn't count
how many 5150 comments

00:11:27.230 --> 00:11:28.380
there were on Amanda's last video

00:11:28.380 --> 00:11:31.640
and it's like the police
have been approached 50 times

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:34.270
about doing a 5150 on
Amanda and they just won't.

00:11:34.270 --> 00:11:37.200
- As we're learning,
there's a lot of corruption

00:11:37.200 --> 00:11:40.520
and a lot of elements
of our judicial system

00:11:40.520 --> 00:11:43.790
and that bleeds down into
LAPD and everywhere else.

00:11:43.790 --> 00:11:45.150
- [Mark] As the sirens go by.

00:11:45.150 --> 00:11:46.600
- As the sirens go by.

00:11:46.600 --> 00:11:48.930
- [Mark] My experience with
the LAPD has been great.

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:51.223
I appreciate what they've done for me,

00:11:52.290 --> 00:11:53.370
they've saved my ass a few times.

00:11:53.370 --> 00:11:55.430
So I have no problems with the police

00:11:55.430 --> 00:11:57.830
but I understand that
it's just a difficult job.

00:12:00.430 --> 00:12:04.820
- It's such an overwhelming
environment here in skid row

00:12:04.820 --> 00:12:09.370
and any other place like
this, that unfortunately,

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:11.376
this is last on the totem pole.

00:12:11.376 --> 00:12:14.590
So if someone does get 5150'd, again,

00:12:14.590 --> 00:12:17.220
they're released after 72 hours.

00:12:17.220 --> 00:12:19.180
The likelihood that they
send them to a facility,

00:12:19.180 --> 00:12:21.030
in which case that's still only 14 days

00:12:21.030 --> 00:12:22.880
and then they're still sent back out,

00:12:25.539 --> 00:12:26.987
it's a huge conversation but-

00:12:26.987 --> 00:12:28.940
- [Mark] And just back me up on this one,

00:12:28.940 --> 00:12:30.370
you know Amanda, you're familiar with her?

00:12:30.370 --> 00:12:31.360
- Yeah, uh-huh.

00:12:31.360 --> 00:12:34.653
- [Mark] Tell me there are not
300 other Amandas out here.

00:12:35.760 --> 00:12:37.430
- I live and work right here

00:12:37.430 --> 00:12:40.090
and I feed a lot of the people that live

00:12:40.090 --> 00:12:41.413
at the back of my street,

00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:47.490
and a lot of people here are
battling mental health issues

00:12:49.150 --> 00:12:49.983
because-

00:12:49.983 --> 00:12:50.816
- [Mark] On the way in this morning,

00:12:50.816 --> 00:12:53.050
that would be a great
male version of Amanda,

00:12:53.050 --> 00:12:54.690
and there was another Amanda and-

00:12:54.690 --> 00:12:56.290
- They're everywhere.

00:12:56.290 --> 00:12:58.560
Because where do they go?

00:12:58.560 --> 00:12:59.393
Where do they go?

00:12:59.393 --> 00:13:03.382
They're either in the jail
system or they're here.

00:13:03.382 --> 00:13:04.215
- [Mark] Or they're here.

00:13:04.215 --> 00:13:07.590
- If they don't have the
means to go handle it.

00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:09.420
- [Mark] Well, what you
guys do, it sounds great.

00:13:09.420 --> 00:13:10.450
Sounds amazing.

00:13:10.450 --> 00:13:11.380
- Yeah.

00:13:11.380 --> 00:13:12.894
I enjoy doing it (laughs)

00:13:12.894 --> 00:13:14.272
- [Mark] We'll see if we can
get one of these young people

00:13:14.272 --> 00:13:18.110
that I've interviewed to maybe sign up

00:13:18.110 --> 00:13:21.283
or try to get into it
and see where it goes.

00:13:23.060 --> 00:13:26.080
So the campaign that
I've got going so far,

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:28.120
it may not be as robust as it could be,

00:13:28.120 --> 00:13:29.400
but it's still very helpful.

00:13:29.400 --> 00:13:31.150
A lot of the people that are over 25,

00:13:31.150 --> 00:13:33.330
that you guys don't really deal with,

00:13:33.330 --> 00:13:35.020
still could benefit and that's
a majority of the people

00:13:35.020 --> 00:13:35.853
I interview anyway.

00:13:35.853 --> 00:13:39.490
Latoya, maybe we can get
her a hotel room for a week.

00:13:39.490 --> 00:13:41.990
Or maybe we can get Caroline
off the street for a while

00:13:41.990 --> 00:13:43.883
or get so and so a new tent.

00:13:46.740 --> 00:13:48.620
There's so many people that
come to me looking for clothes,

00:13:48.620 --> 00:13:51.410
they're looking for shoes,
they need money for food.

00:13:51.410 --> 00:13:53.180
So the donations are still useful,

00:13:53.180 --> 00:13:57.660
even if it's a few hundred dollars a day

00:13:57.660 --> 00:13:59.740
that are coming in now,
that's still very helpful

00:13:59.740 --> 00:14:02.060
because that'll make a lot of these people

00:14:02.060 --> 00:14:04.100
that you see on my channel,
it'll make their lives

00:14:04.100 --> 00:14:06.270
more comfortable, more pleasant

00:14:06.270 --> 00:14:08.900
and I'm sure they'll
appreciate that, as I do,

00:14:08.900 --> 00:14:11.473
because otherwise it comes
out of my pocket entirely.

00:14:14.690 --> 00:14:15.740
And maybe who knows?

00:14:15.740 --> 00:14:18.010
Maybe some miracle will happen
and we'll get more support

00:14:18.010 --> 00:14:19.290
of this campaign.

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:22.501
I'm not big on promoting it,
so that's part of the problem.

00:14:22.501 --> 00:14:23.970
(laughing)

00:14:23.970 --> 00:14:26.350
I have a hard time telling people

00:14:26.350 --> 00:14:28.040
to hit the subscribe button-

00:14:28.040 --> 00:14:29.821
- Please subscribe!

00:14:29.821 --> 00:14:30.654
Listen!

00:14:30.654 --> 00:14:31.487
- [Mark] Don't forget to donate.

00:14:31.487 --> 00:14:32.991
- This is important work!

00:14:32.991 --> 00:14:33.824
- [Mark] It's not in my personality.

00:14:33.824 --> 00:14:35.720
- [Monika] This is important work.

00:14:35.720 --> 00:14:40.280
This is a really big problem
that this country has

00:14:40.280 --> 00:14:42.930
and we have the opportunity,

00:14:42.930 --> 00:14:45.080
for the first time that
I've seen on a large scale

00:14:45.080 --> 00:14:47.457
with what you've already got going on,

00:14:47.457 --> 00:14:48.710
in a short period of
time, to bring awareness

00:14:51.967 --> 00:14:55.090
to the human beings
that are really hurting

00:14:55.090 --> 00:14:58.750
and that we really have
not set them up to win.

00:14:58.750 --> 00:15:01.170
But we have an opportunity to shift that,

00:15:01.170 --> 00:15:03.327
so let's fuckin' shift it.

00:15:03.327 --> 00:15:05.820
- [Mark] (laughs) Awesome.

00:15:05.820 --> 00:15:07.050
Monika, thank you so much for coming in.

00:15:07.050 --> 00:15:07.883
- [Monika] No problem.

00:15:07.883 --> 00:15:08.716
- [Mark] I look forward
to working with you.

00:15:08.716 --> 00:15:09.549
- [Monika] Me too.

00:15:09.549 --> 00:15:10.382
- [Mark] Thanks.

